## Conventions
- API: see `context/api-conventions.md`. Errors use `{ error: { code, message, details? } }`.
- Tests: see `context/testing-standards.md`.
- Files `kebab-case`; JSON fields exactly as in `CONTRACT.md`.

## Known structural problems
- [Describe current debt honestly so Claude doesn't copy it — e.g. "routes.js is 2,000 lines; new routes go in src/routes/<resource>.ts".]

## Never do
- Never commit with failing or skipped tests.
- Never read or write `.env*` files (except `.env.example`); never hard-code credentials.
- Never invent an endpoint, field or error code that isn't in `CONTRACT.md` — change the contract first.
- [Project-specific prohibitions, each with a one-line reason.]

## Verification policy
- After every atomic unit: `/verify-unit [scope]` must report `UNIT VERIFIED`, then `/ship-unit`.
- Before merging a branch: `/verify-app`, then `/audit` for feature-sized work.
- A deploy command is not proof; production is verified by exercising live routes.

## Supporting documents (read when relevant — not every session)
| File | What | Read when |
|---|---|---|
| `PRD.md` | Product, users, success criteria | Scoping or prioritising |
| `CONTRACT.md` | Endpoints, shapes, error codes, acceptance criteria | Any API or data work |
| `BUILD_SEQUENCE.md` | Ordered atomic units + "verified when" | Starting or finishing a unit |
| `docs/DESIGN_SPEC.md`, `docs/DESIGN.md` (or `docs/DESIGN_STANDARD.md`), `docs/MOTION_BRIEF.md` | UI states / visual system / motion | Any UI work (delete if API-only) |
| `AUDIT_LOG.md` | Past audit findings and resolutions | Before an audit or release |

